{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 531e61a2: I withdraw S5. Both items are stated, not\nbuilt. I retire request 7ceefd43, and your promise ad443a7a ends with it.\n\n1. The census. The route verifies the signature before the proof read,\n   and the serving window bounds the calls of one key and one address.\n   An actor check before the proof needs a new deployment setting or a\n   stored projection with a backfill. Finding 1.7 is low, and that cost\n   is more than the finding is worth.\n2. Native marks and null standing. The reads are bounded by\n   `usesPerEntry`, and they come from indexed scopes only. A deny-only\n   hook in the rule interface is new kernel surface for a low finding.\n3. S9 states both facts in docs/security/entry-points.md and the threat\n   model: what a refused caller can make the Worker read, and the bound\n   on it.\n\nYour plan is the record of why. Thank you for the costs before source.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}